# The themed keyword in front of an operation is optional — the compiler
# infers it from the phrase. This is example 01 written without a single
# prefix, and it resolves to exactly the same pipeline (quickselect and all;
# run it with --explain).
#
# The two spellings mix freely: the Filter below keeps its keyword, and every
# other line drops it. A Shikigami is called by its bare name too, which is
# why a Shikigami may not be named after a built-in operation.
#
#   domain examples/16_no_prefixes.domain
#   Expected output: 15000
Shikigami "Heavy Elves"
    Filter
        Using: (g) -> sum(g) > 5000

16_no_prefixes.input
Split Text by "\n\n"
Split Each by "\n"
Convert Each List to Integers
Heavy Elves
Sum Each Group
Count Equals 3
Quicksort, Descending
Cursed Technique: Take Item 0
stdout
